帕姆·哈珀特发布了一条动态，介绍了塞西莉亚·玛丽·哈珀特，

147
00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.140
weighing in at 7 pounds and 2 ounces.
体重7磅2盎司。

148
00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:25.980
Aw.
噢。

149
00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.320
Yeah, isn't that cute?
是啊，这不可爱吗？

150
00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.520
And I'll put that in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

151
00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:35.980
Well, I remember that they would have me write little things about how baby Cece was doing.
我记得他们会让我写一些关于小Cece近况的小短文。

152
00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:44.780
It was a way that when Pam was on maternity leave, there was still activity from that character, at least as far as the blog.
这样当Pam休产假时，那个角色至少在博客上还能保持活跃度。

153
00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:45.440
Yeah.
是啊。

154
00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:45.880
Yeah.
没错。

155
00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.800
Well, the birth announcement was really cute.
出生公告写得真的很可爱。

156
00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:49.440
All right.
好的。

157
00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.740
Fast fact number two is a location breakdown.
第二个冷知识是关于拍摄地点的。

158
00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:58.720
Jim and Pam give birth at Moses Taylor Hospital, which is a real hospital in Scranton.
Jim和Pam是在摩西泰勒医院生孩子的，那是斯克兰顿真实存在的一家医院。

159
00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:03.160
But of course, we did not shoot at the real Moses Taylor Hospital.
但我们当然不是在真正的摩西泰勒医院拍摄的。

160
00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:08.720
The exterior of the hospital we shot at was St. Joseph Hospital in Burbank, California.
我们拍摄的医院外观是加州伯班克的圣约瑟夫医院。

161
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.860
But the interiors were built over on our warehouse set.
但内部场景是在我们的仓库摄影棚里搭建的。

162
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.920
The entire hospital set, the waiting room, the hospital room, the hallways, all of it.
整个医院场景，候诊室、病房、走廊，全都是。

163
00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.020
I mean, the detail.
我是说，那些细节。

164
00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:20.900
Amazing.
太惊人了。

165
00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:26.080
Randy shared with me that they had torn down the Dunder Mifflin, New York offices
Randy跟我说，他们拆掉了邓德·米夫林纽约办公室的布景，

166
00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.500
because we don't need them anymore.
因为我们不再需要它们了。

167
00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.340
And in their place, they built the hospital.
取而代之的是，他们搭建了医院场景。

168
00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:37.960
So the other big storyline in this episode involves Dwight destroying Jim and Pam's kitchen.
这一集里另一条重要的故事线是Dwight拆毁了Jim和Pam的厨房。

169
00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:44.040
Rather than go destroy someone's house, our set designer, Michael Gallenberg,
为了不用真的去毁掉谁的房子，我们的布景设计师Michael Gallenberg，

170
00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:50.320
took photos and measurements of the original location house that we had used for Jim and Pam's house
拍下了我们之前用作Jim和Pam家那处实景房子的照片并进行了测量，

171
00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:56.480
and then they meticulously recreated the floor plan also on our warehouse set.
然后他们也在我们的仓库摄影棚里一丝不苟地重建了那个户型图。

172
00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.200
They built basically two structures.
他们基本上搭建了两个建筑结构。

173
00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.340
They built a hospital and a house.
一个是医院，一个是房子。

174
00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:02.260
Yes.
是的。

175
00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.740
It was constructed by Tim James and decorated by Steve Rothstein.
它是由Tim James建造，并由Steve Rothstein负责装饰的。

176
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.800
It's funny, Angela, like you said, they were right next to each other.
真有趣，Angela，就像你说的，它们就在彼此隔壁。

177
00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:17.100
When Isabel, the character of Isabel, goes from the hospital to Jim and Pam's house,
当Isabel这个角色从医院去到Jim和Pam家时，

178
00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.600
she really did not have to walk very far.
她其实根本不用走多远。

179
00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:20.820
No, just around the corner.
没错，就在拐角处。

180
00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:21.220
It was.
确实是。

181
00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.520
We shot those on the same day, and it was very easy for her.
我们是在同一天拍摄的，这对她来说非常方便。

182
00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:32.520
And when I was going back and forth with Randy about these locations, he told me a very fun tidbit.
当我和Randy沟通这些拍摄地点时，他告诉了我一个非常有趣的小花絮。

183
00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:37.160
Angela, do you remember that little kitchen outside of our writer's offices?
Angela，你还记得我们编剧办公室外面的那个小厨房吗？

184
00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.160
By the back stairwell?
就在后楼梯旁边那个？

185
00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:39.740
Yeah.
记得。

186
00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:40.140
Yeah.
是啊。

187
00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:41.800
I mean, it wasn't really a kitchen.
其实那算不上真正的厨房。

188
00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:46.180
It was almost just like a pantry kind of thing.
那几乎就是一个储藏室之类的东西。

189
00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.000
It was like a shelf.
就像个架子一样。

190
00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.140
They'd put food on it.
他们会把食物放在上面。

191
00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.300
It wasn't really a kitchen.
那真的不是厨房。

192
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:56.860
No, they had an old refrigerator, but there was not any, like, sink or working plumbing or any appliances.
没错，他们有个旧冰箱，但没有任何水槽、自来水管道或任何电器。

193
00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.500
There was, I think, a toaster oven, maybe a microwave.
我想有个烤箱，可能还有个微波炉。

194
00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.200
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，没错。

195
00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.940
It was kind of a sad kitchen.
那是个挺寒酸的厨房。

196
00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:02.820
It was sad.
确实很寒酸。

197
00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:10.680
Well, when this script came up, Randy said he saw these beats of Dwight demolishing the Halpert kitchen,
当这个剧本出来时，Randy说他看到了Dwight拆毁Halpert家厨房的这些情节，

198
00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:14.160
and his, quote, mental wheels started turning.
然后他，引用他的话，脑子开始飞速运转了。

199
00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.320
Oh, Randy.
噢，Randy。

200
00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:21.820
See, he thought, what if we bought enough cabinets for several takes of the Halpert
你看，他在想，如果我们买足够的橱柜来应付Halpert家厨房的多次拍摄会怎样

201
00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:27.960
kitchen, but then had enough left over to remodel and refurbish the writer's kitchen?
厨房，但剩下的材料又足够去翻新和整修编剧室的厨房？

202
00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:33.760
So he spoke to Michael Gallenberg and Steve Rothstein, and when the episode wrapped, over
于是他找了迈克尔·加伦伯格和史蒂夫·罗斯坦谈了谈，等那集拍完后的

203
00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:40.040
the subsequent weekend, they had a construction crew scheduled to, like, come strike the Halpert
那个周末，他们就安排了一支施工队，去把哈尔珀特家的

204
00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:40.480
kitchen.
厨房拆了。

205
00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:46.000
And that same crew brought that extra cabinetry and flooring to the writer's kitchen,
同一支施工队把多出来的橱柜和地板带到了编剧室的厨房，

206
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.540
and they completely remodeled it over one weekend.
并在那个周末把它彻底翻新了一遍。

207
00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.920
So when the writers came to work the following
所以当编剧们在接下来的

208
00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:58.200
Monday, they were greeted by, quote, a spotless, pristine, and sanitary kitchen with plenty of
周一上班时，迎接他们的是一个“一尘不染、崭新且卫生”的厨房，有充足的

209
00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.440
counter space to lay out their lunch choices.
台面空间来摆放他们的午餐。

210
00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.860
He said the dishwasher that had been in the
他说，原本在哈尔珀特家

211
00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:09.380
Halpert kitchen was installed in the adjacent hallway where there was an existing sink and
厨房里的洗碗机被安装在了隔壁走廊，那里本来就有水槽和

212
00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:09.740
plumbing.
管道。

213
00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.340
They added a garbage disposal.
他们还加装了一个垃圾处理器。

214
00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:15.560
So after six seasons, the writers had a clean space to
就这样，六季之后，编剧们终于有了一个干净的空间来

215
00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:19.500
keep food, and the PAs had a garbage disposal and dishwasher to wash up.
存放食物，制片助理们也有了垃圾处理器和洗碗机来清洗餐具。

216
00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.000
Randy said he cleverly
兰迪说他很聪明地

217
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.280
buried the costs in the episode's budget.
把这些费用隐藏在了那一集的预算里。

218
00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.540
It was a win-win for everyone.
这对每个人来说都是双赢。

219
00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.140
I remember this.
我记得这件事。

220
00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:28.960
I remember
我现在听你提起，

221
00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.160
this now that you're sharing it.
我记起来了。

222
00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:34.740
I remember how excited the writers were to have a real kitchen.
我记得编剧们当时能拥有一个真正的厨房有多兴奋。

223
00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:35.500
Yeah.
是啊。

224
00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.420
But I never knew how it came about or anything like that.
但我从来不知道这事是怎么促成的，或者类似的细节。

225
00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.020
Randy always was looking out.
兰迪总是很会照顾人。

226
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.300
That is such a great story.
这故事真棒。

227
00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:49.020
It is such a good example of how he was always trying to make every person's life on set a little better however he could.
这很好地体现了他总是尽其所能让片场每个人的生活变得更好一点。

228
00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:49.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

229
00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:50.740
All right.
好了。

230
00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.360
Fast fact number three, Angela.
第三个冷知识，安吉拉。

231
00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:56.400
We had two pretty big guest stars on this show.
我们这集有两位非常重量级的客串明星。

232
00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.580
First up, Sarah Baker as Nurse Josie.
首先是饰演乔西护士的莎拉·贝克。

233
00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:04.760
She was born in D.C., raised in Springfield, Virginia.
她出生于华盛顿特区，在弗吉尼亚州的斯普林菲尔德长大。

234
00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:08.560
She studied theater and English at James Madison University.
她在詹姆斯麦迪逊大学学习了戏剧和英语。

235
00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:14.760
She went on to practice improv at Whole World Improv Theater as both a student and teacher.
后来她在“全世界即兴剧场”练习即兴表演，既是学生也是老师。

236
00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.840
She continued studying performing at the Groundlings after moving to Los Angeles,
搬到洛杉矶后，她继续在“接地气剧团”学习表演，

237
00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:25.620
and she has appeared in numerous films and television shows, such as The Campaign, starring Will Ferrell,
她出演过许多电影和电视剧，比如威尔·法瑞尔主演的《政坛混战》，

238
00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:29.200
Goliath, Better Things, The Kaminsky Method, and Will & Grace.
还有《律政巨人》、《更美好的事》、《柯明斯基理论》和《威尔和格蕾丝》。

239
00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:33.780
And she was nominated for a Critics' Choice Award for her guest starring role on Louie.
她还凭借在《路易不容易》中的客串角色获得了评论家选择奖提名。

240
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.100
She just crushed it.
她演得太棒了。

241
00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:35.820
She was amazing.
她太惊艳了。

242
00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:36.760
She was so good.
她演得真好。

243
00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:42.040
I mean, some of the looks that she gives to Jim and Pam are so good.
我是说，她看向吉姆和帕姆的一些眼神戏太精彩了。

244
00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.660
Her chemistry with John Krasinski was amazing.
她和约翰·卡拉辛斯基之间的化学反应太棒了。

245
00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.300
I know.
我知道。

246
00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:52.860
I mean, I would just sit there in between them as they were giving their just gentle, snarky sass.
我是说，我就坐在他们中间，看着他们互相抛出那种温和又带刺的俏皮话。

247
00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.140
It was so much fun.
太有趣了。

248
00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:02.360
And our second big guest star is Lee Kirk as our lactation consultant, Clark.
我们的第二位大牌客串明星是饰演哺乳顾问克拉克的李·柯克。

249
00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:03.860
Your husband.
你丈夫。

250
00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:05.020
My husband.
我丈夫。

251
00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:06.400
Exactly.
没错。

252
00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:11.860
So we were engaged to be married when he played Clark.
所以在他扮演克拉克的时候，我们已经订婚了。

253
00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:14.560
And he is going to come on the show today.
他今天会来参加节目。

254
00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.300
And we're going to get to talk to him all about that experience.
我们到时候会和他好好聊聊那段经历。

255
00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:19.440
He did so great.
他演得太棒了。

256
00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.900
I can't wait to talk to him.
我迫不及待想和他聊聊了。

257
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.100
I have a few questions for him.
我还有几个问题要问他。

258
00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:27.240
I think our listeners know Lee as a person who makes amazing eggs and coffee.
我想我们的听众都知道李是个会做美味鸡蛋和咖啡的人。

259
00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:30.100
They also know that he's a writer-director.
他们也知道他是一位编剧兼导演。

260
00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:35.820
But what you might not know about him is that he did attend the Goodman School for acting in Chicago.
但你们可能不知道的是，他确实在芝加哥的古德曼戏剧学院学过表演。

261
00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:43.300
So acting in this episode was not too big of a leap for him, even though ultimately now he is a writer-director.
所以对他来说，在这一集中表演并不是什么太大的跨越，尽管他现在主要是一名编剧兼导演。

262
00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:46.840
And, you know, Lee was supposed to come into the studio with us today.
而且，你知道，李本来今天应该和我们一起进录音室的。

263
00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:50.200
We were so excited, but our daughter woke up not feeling great.
我们本来很兴奋，但我们的女儿醒来时感觉不太舒服。

264
00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:57.360
So she stayed home from school, he's staying home with her, and we're actually going to have to talk to my own husband, but over a Zoom.
所以她没去上学，他在家陪她，我们实际上得通过Zoom和我自己的丈夫连线。

265
00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:59.040
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

266
00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.700
He's going to be here, and it's going to be super fun.
他会来的，这一定会非常有趣。

267
00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:04.340
I'm just so excited that he's going to be on the show.
我真的太高兴他能上节目了。

268
00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:04.900
Yeah.
是啊。

269
00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.260
It's going to be kind of cool.
这会很酷的。

270
00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:13.040
All right, well, we're going to take a break, and when we come back, we'll break down this first part of the episode, and then later, we'll talk to Clark.
好了，我们要休息一下，回来后，我们将剖析这一集的第一部分，稍后再和克拉克聊聊。

271
00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:22.660
Well, we're back.
好了，我们回来了。

272
00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:28.200
Jim went to get himself ice chips because he kind of got a little dizzy there for a minute.
吉姆去给自己拿冰块了，因为他刚才有一会儿觉得有点头晕。

273
00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.340
He might have passed out a little bit.
他可能差点晕过去了。

274
00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:29.820
He might have passed out, yeah.
他可能确实晕了一下，没错。

275
00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:36.840
Well, I don't know if you notice when he comes through those automatic doors at 26 seconds, those are fakie doors.
嗯，不知道你们有没有注意到，当他在26秒时穿过那些自动门时，那是假门。

276
00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:38.820
Those were not automatic.
那些不是自动的。

277
00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.880
Just like our elevator, that's some movie magic for you.
就像我们的电梯一样，这就是电影魔术。

278
00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:50.480
Randy Cordray told me that they were operated by our grips who had to pull on cables in unison.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我，它们是由我们的场务操作的，他们必须齐心协力拉动缆绳。

279
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:59.060
Each door was being pulled by a different person, and they would get a cue on a walkie-talkie from our first AD who was watching the action live.
每扇门都由不同的人拉动，他们会通过对讲机从现场观看拍摄的第一副导演那里得到指令。

280
00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.420
Well, they did great because you would never know.
嗯，他们做得很好，因为你根本看不出来。

281
00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:02.140
Never know.
根本看不出来。

282
00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.200
They timed it perfectly.
他们配合得天衣无缝。

283
00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:08.240
Well, Michael is going to arrive with, I think, all the balloons they had in the store that day.
迈克尔带着我想是那天店里所有的气球赶到了。

284
00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:08.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

285
00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.260
I mean, there's so many, and they're huge.
