不工作的时候可以和父母待在那里。

596
00:29:02.260 --> 00:29:04.520
And they are assigned a nurse.
而且他们还配有一名护士。

597
00:29:04.740 --> 00:29:06.880
Yes, that accompanies them to the set.
是的，护士会陪同他们去片场。

598
00:29:06.980 --> 00:29:07.320
Correct.
没错。

599
00:29:07.900 --> 00:29:11.220
And this is why we needed two sets of twins
这就是为什么我们需要两对双胞胎，

600
00:29:11.220 --> 00:29:16.200
because that way we had 80 minutes of on-camera baby time total.
因为这样我们总共就有80分钟的宝宝出镜时间了。

601
00:29:16.440 --> 00:29:19.660
We also used a fakie baby,
我们还用了一个假婴儿，

602
00:29:19.660 --> 00:29:27.500
which we called jelly baby and creepy baby they are really creepy they are made from kind of a
我们叫它果冻宝宝和恐怖宝宝，它们真的很恐怖，是用一种

603
00:29:27.500 --> 00:29:34.440
soft pliable cast polymer you shared on the commentary that they were actually heavier
柔软易弯曲的铸造聚合物做的，你在评论音轨里分享过它们其实比

604
00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:41.040
than the real babies yes and their heads were super floppy so you actually had to um like hold their
真婴儿还要重，是的，而且它们的头特别软，所以你实际上得，嗯，像

605
00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:47.020
heads just like a real baby yeah but they were much heavier and it was jelly they were gelatinous
抱真婴儿一样托着它们的头，对，但它们重得多，而且是果冻状的，它们是凝胶质地的。

606
00:29:47.020 --> 00:29:47.660
Yeah.
是啊。

607
00:29:48.080 --> 00:29:49.520
I mean, it was weird.
我的意思是，那真的很怪。

608
00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:52.680
It's the same people, I think, that made Fakie Bandit.
我想应该是同一拨人做的假班迪特。

609
00:29:53.080 --> 00:29:53.360
Yeah.
是啊。

610
00:29:53.640 --> 00:29:55.260
And he was a jelly cat.
而且它是一只果冻猫。

611
00:29:55.820 --> 00:29:56.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

612
00:29:56.220 --> 00:29:56.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

613
00:29:56.860 --> 00:30:05.440
You also shared on the commentary that at 8 minutes, 52 seconds, when the nurse rolls Cece out of the room, you know, she's in her crib and she's going to roll her out.
你还在评论音轨里提到，在8分52秒时，当护士把西西推离房间，你知道，她躺在婴儿床里，护士要把她推走。

614
00:30:05.580 --> 00:30:05.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

615
00:30:06.040 --> 00:30:07.100
That's the fake baby.
那是假婴儿。

616
00:30:07.360 --> 00:30:09.860
If you go back and watch, it's not even moving at all.
如果你回去看的话，它根本动都不动。

617
00:30:10.460 --> 00:30:11.020
Yes.
是的。

618
00:30:11.280 --> 00:30:17.780
I believe we also used Fakie Baby in a good portion of the scene with Clark.
我相信我们在和克拉克的那场戏里也用了很大一部分假婴儿。

619
00:30:18.200 --> 00:30:22.460
You might notice you don't really ever see a baby there.
你可能会注意到你其实从来没在那儿看到过婴儿。

620
00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:22.980
Right.
没错。

621
00:30:23.700 --> 00:30:24.000
Yeah.
是啊。

622
00:30:24.580 --> 00:30:26.920
Should we talk about what Dwight is doing now?
我们要聊聊德怀特现在在做什么吗？

623
00:30:27.340 --> 00:30:28.680
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

624
00:30:28.680 --> 00:30:31.760
He couldn't find the iPod, but guess what he found?
他没找到iPod，但你猜他找到了什么？

625
00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:32.900
Mold.
霉菌。

626
00:30:33.160 --> 00:30:34.360
And a lot of it.
而且是一大堆。

627
00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:35.140
Yeah.
是啊。

628
00:30:35.300 --> 00:30:38.940
He wants to solve this mold problem for them, but first he needs to do,
他想帮他们解决这个霉菌问题，但首先他需要做，

629
00:30:38.940 --> 00:30:42.200
I mean, obviously, what anyone would do.
我的意思是，很明显，任何正常人都会做的事。

630
00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:42.560
Right.
没错。

631
00:30:42.760 --> 00:30:46.560
If you show up to tackle mold, you read a book, you take a bath in someone's bathtub.
如果你去处理霉菌，你会读本书，在别人的浴缸里洗个澡。

632
00:30:46.720 --> 00:30:47.680
You sleep in their bed.
睡在他们的床上。

633
00:30:47.780 --> 00:30:50.060
Without any undies.
还不穿内裤。

634
00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:50.460
BottoMs.
底部。

635
00:30:50.660 --> 00:30:51.120
Yeah.
是啊。

636
00:30:51.420 --> 00:30:53.580
Commando, question for you.
不穿内裤，问你个问题。

637
00:30:54.400 --> 00:30:57.880
Did the documentary crew stay overnight at Jim and Pam's?
纪录片摄制组在吉姆和帕姆家过夜了吗？

638
00:30:57.900 --> 00:30:58.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

639
00:30:59.180 --> 00:31:01.860
How many cameramen do they have on this day?
他们那天有多少摄影师？

640
00:31:02.100 --> 00:31:04.280
What's their budget for this documentary?
这部纪录片的预算是多少？

641
00:31:04.580 --> 00:31:06.340
They've got cameras back at the office.
他们在办公室里有摄像机。

642
00:31:06.340 --> 00:31:08.120
They've got some over in the hospital.
他们在医院那边也有一些。

643
00:31:08.120 --> 00:31:10.100
They're following Dwight as well.
他们也在跟着德怀特。

644
00:31:10.240 --> 00:31:10.480
Yeah.
是啊。

645
00:31:10.680 --> 00:31:11.500
They are committed.
他们真是太敬业了。

646
00:31:12.140 --> 00:31:23.400
I wanted to point out that at five minutes, one second, that exterior shot of Dwight breaking into Jim and Pam's house, I mean, he literally elbows the window and it breaks.
我想指出在5分01秒，德怀特闯入吉姆和帕姆家的那个外景镜头，我的意思是，他真的是用手肘撞破了窗户。

647
00:31:23.640 --> 00:31:25.500
Right, because he doesn't want to know where the keys are.
没错，因为他不想知道钥匙在哪儿。

648
00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:26.820
La, la, la, la, la, la.
啦，啦，啦，啦，啦，啦。

649
00:31:26.840 --> 00:31:27.320
Don't, no.
别，不。

650
00:31:27.340 --> 00:31:27.520
No.
不。

651
00:31:27.640 --> 00:31:28.140
Don't tell me.
别告诉我。

652
00:31:28.240 --> 00:31:29.040
He's going to get in.
他要进去了。

653
00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:29.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

654
00:31:29.940 --> 00:31:31.680
First of all, that was breakaway glass.
首先，那是易碎玻璃。

655
00:31:31.980 --> 00:31:36.140
But second of all, that was also built on our stages.
但其次，那也是在我们摄影棚里搭建的。

656
00:31:36.140 --> 00:31:43.680
That exterior, they literally rebuilt the exterior of that real house to do just that little break-in bit.
那个外观，他们为了拍那一点点闯入的戏份，真的把那栋房子的外观给重建了。

657
00:31:43.920 --> 00:31:45.720
It is lit so well.
灯光打得真好。

658
00:31:46.380 --> 00:31:49.460
I mean, our set builders had a very busy week.
我是说，我们的布景师那周可忙坏了。

659
00:31:49.700 --> 00:31:49.920
Yeah.
是啊。

660
00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:57.500
There's going to be another thing that I'm going to talk about later where we fake outside and we actually shot it on the warehouse set.
后面我还会提到另一件事，我们伪造了室外场景，实际上是在仓库摄影棚里拍的。

661
00:31:57.580 --> 00:32:04.920
And I just have to give a shout out to our lighting crew because they really made these places look like we were outside, but really we were in a warehouse.
我必须得给我们的灯光组点个赞，因为他们真的让这些地方看起来像是在室外，但其实我们是在仓库里。

662
00:32:05.380 --> 00:32:08.120
Well, listen, Dwight is well-rested.
听着，德怀特休息得很好。

663
00:32:08.300 --> 00:32:09.360
He's ready to get to work.
他准备好开工了。

664
00:32:09.540 --> 00:32:14.000
He's going to demo their kitchen to get rid of the mold.
他要去拆掉他们的厨房来除霉。

665
00:32:14.340 --> 00:32:14.620
Yeah.
是啊。

666
00:32:14.860 --> 00:32:20.440
So on the commentary, they shared that that side of the cabinet where he swings the sledgehammer.
所以在评论音轨里，他们分享说他挥舞大锤砸的那个橱柜侧面。

667
00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:20.900
Yeah.
是啊。

668
00:32:21.040 --> 00:32:24.780
They had scored it a little so that when he hit it, it would, like, break apart.
他们提前刻了痕，这样他一砸，它就会碎掉。

669
00:32:24.920 --> 00:32:25.160
Okay.
好吧。

670
00:32:25.760 --> 00:32:26.920
It wouldn't break apart.
结果它没碎。

671
00:32:27.280 --> 00:32:27.680
What?
什么？

672
00:32:27.820 --> 00:32:30.660
He swung that thing and hit it several times, and nothing happened.
他抡起那玩意儿砸了好几下，结果什么事都没发生。

673
00:32:31.220 --> 00:32:35.640
So it was actually really hard to get a shot of them really whacking into that thing.
所以要拍到他们真正砸烂那东西的镜头其实非常困难。

674
00:32:36.100 --> 00:32:37.320
That's so funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

675
00:32:37.440 --> 00:32:41.780
I mean, he could crush an apple with his bare hands, but they couldn't get that cabinet to break.
我是说，他能徒手捏碎苹果，但他们却没法让那个橱柜碎掉。

676
00:32:41.920 --> 00:32:44.580
Well, it must have been a really sturdy cabinet.
看来那一定是个非常结实的橱柜。

677
00:32:45.940 --> 00:32:49.060
Should we go back to Dunder Mifflin and see what everyone else is doing?
我们要回到邓德·米夫林看看其他人都在干什么吗？

678
00:32:49.420 --> 00:32:50.980
Oh, we definitely should.
哦，我们绝对应该回去看看。

679
00:32:51.880 --> 00:32:59.180
Michael is doing that thing where he is taking responsibility for something he had nothing to do with.
迈克尔又在做那种事了，把一件跟他毫无关系的事情揽到自己身上。

680
00:32:59.340 --> 00:33:00.500
Oh, Jim and Pam.
哦，吉姆和帕姆。

681
00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:01.540
He's the matchmaker.
他是红娘。

682
00:33:01.740 --> 00:33:02.240
He is.
没错。

683
00:33:02.380 --> 00:33:05.560
And he's going to start matching up everyone in the office.
他打算开始撮合办公室里的每一个人。

684
00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:06.520
That's right.
确实。

685
00:33:06.900 --> 00:33:09.120
This scene had a series of talking heads.
这一幕有一系列采访镜头。

686
00:33:09.640 --> 00:33:10.620
First was Meredith.
首先是梅雷迪斯。

687
00:33:10.820 --> 00:33:12.520
You know, she said she's single, obviously.
你知道，她显然说了她是单身。

688
00:33:12.520 --> 00:33:13.960
She's never getting married.
她永远不会结婚。

689
00:33:14.140 --> 00:33:16.020
And her talking head is like Clooney.
而她的采访镜头就像克鲁尼一样。

690
00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:18.900
Meredith is our office's George Clooney.
梅雷迪斯就是我们办公室的乔治·克鲁尼。

691
00:33:19.060 --> 00:33:19.220
Yeah.
是啊。

692
00:33:19.420 --> 00:33:19.720
Who knew?
谁能想到呢？

693
00:33:20.460 --> 00:33:23.240
Andy has one, of course, where he talks about Aaron.
安迪当然也有一个，他在里面谈到了艾琳。

694
00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:25.440
He's hoping the stars will align for them.
他希望他们能有缘分。

695
00:33:25.580 --> 00:33:28.220
And then, Jenna, would have come creeds.
然后，珍娜，接下来是克里德的。

696
00:33:28.220 --> 00:33:34.760
Remember this deleted runner I shared with you that he thought if Jim and Pam had their baby, that meant he was going to die?
还记得我跟你分享过那个被删减的连贯情节吗？他以为如果吉姆和帕姆生了孩子，就意味着他要死了？

697
00:33:34.960 --> 00:33:35.420
Yes.
记得。

698
00:33:35.700 --> 00:33:35.940
Okay.
好吧。

699
00:33:36.400 --> 00:33:39.720
Well, now Pam has had the baby and he's still alive.
现在帕姆已经生了孩子，而他还活着。

700
00:33:40.420 --> 00:33:42.300
Here's Creed's deleted talking head.
这是克里德被删减的采访镜头。

701
00:33:42.840 --> 00:33:45.440
Pam and her baby, and I'm still alive.
帕姆和她的宝宝，而我还活着。

702
00:33:46.180 --> 00:33:47.820
I have a new lease on life.
我获得了新生。

703
00:33:48.220 --> 00:33:52.700
If death can't stop me from dating, then neither can my mother.
如果死亡都不能阻止我约会，那我妈也别想。

704
00:33:53.620 --> 00:33:54.140
What?
什么？

705
00:33:56.050 --> 00:33:59.070
And she's still alive and she doesn't want him to date?
她还活着，而且不想让他约会？

706
00:33:59.070 --> 00:34:00.550
I have so many questions.
我有太多问题了。

707
00:34:01.630 --> 00:34:10.290
Well, listen, bottom line, Michael is going to fill all of their empty holes with love.
好吧，听着，归根结底，迈克尔要用爱去填补他们内心的空虚。

708
00:34:10.750 --> 00:34:13.330
With another body and love.
用另一个身体和爱。

709
00:34:13.470 --> 00:34:13.970
Yes.
没错。

710
00:34:14.210 --> 00:34:17.790
And Angela, your look when he says that is so funny.
还有安吉拉，他这么说的时候你的表情太搞笑了。

711
00:34:18.590 --> 00:34:19.850
It's so good.
太棒了。

712
00:34:21.330 --> 00:34:25.790
So Jim and Pam are reminiscing about when they were just a couple of kids,
吉姆和帕姆在回忆他们还是孩子的时候，

713
00:34:26.030 --> 00:34:28.810
afraid to be parents, and here they are holding their baby.
害怕当父母，而现在他们正抱着自己的宝宝。

714
00:34:29.070 --> 00:34:36.330
Oh, it's so peaceful, and they're just laying there together in a sweet little snuggle, staring into her cute little sleeping face.
哦，那画面太宁静了，他们就这样依偎在一起，盯着她可爱的小睡脸。

715
00:34:36.470 --> 00:34:39.110
Yeah, and the nurse is like, would you like us to take her?
是啊，护士问，需要我们把她带走吗？

716
00:34:39.410 --> 00:34:40.970
Yeah, and Jim and Pam say no.
然后吉姆和帕姆说不。

717
00:34:41.370 --> 00:34:43.390
No, no, no, she can just stay here with us.
不，不，不，她可以留在这里陪我们。

718
00:34:43.550 --> 00:34:47.110
Yeah, and this, of course, cuts to Cecilia crying.
是啊，当然，镜头一转，塞西莉亚就在哭。

719
00:34:47.110 --> 00:34:49.390
They're struggling to breastfeed, to swaddle.
他们正为母乳喂养和包裹婴儿而挣扎。

720
00:34:49.590 --> 00:34:50.910
The wheels are coming off the bus.
一切都乱套了。

721
00:34:51.210 --> 00:34:54.830
I have a very funny story about that swaddling moment.
关于那个包裹婴儿的片段，我有个非常有趣的故事。

722
00:34:56.050 --> 00:34:59.870
So we were supposed to not swaddle the baby.
我们当时被要求不要包裹那个婴儿。

723
00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:02.110
That's the joke, is that Jim and Pam.
笑点就在于吉姆和帕姆。

724
00:35:02.270 --> 00:35:02.970
Don't know how.
根本不会。

725
00:35:03.250 --> 00:35:03.570
Yes.
没错。

726
00:35:03.730 --> 00:35:04.510
They need the nurse.
他们需要护士。

727
00:35:04.590 --> 00:35:05.450
We're overwhelmed.
我们不知所措。

728
00:35:05.690 --> 00:35:05.850
Right.
对。

729
00:35:06.370 --> 00:35:10.330
Lady, every time we just swaddled that baby perfectly.
天哪，每次我们都把那个婴儿包裹得完美无缺。

730
00:35:10.590 --> 00:35:11.230
The two of you?
你们俩？

731
00:35:11.330 --> 00:35:11.850
The two of us.
我们俩。

732
00:35:11.970 --> 00:35:12.990
It was insane.
太疯狂了。

733
00:35:12.990 --> 00:35:15.690
We were trying to be bad at swaddling.
我们当时试图表现得不擅长包裹婴儿。

734
00:35:15.830 --> 00:35:17.030
Neither one of us had kids.
我们俩当时都没有孩子。

735
00:35:17.270 --> 00:35:20.330
And somehow we were like masterful swaddlers.
但不知怎么的，我们成了包裹婴儿的高手。

736
00:35:20.750 --> 00:35:26.530
And Harold Ramis and our AD, they kept saying, guys, stop swaddling the baby.
哈罗德·雷米斯和我们的助理导演一直说，伙计们，别再包裹那个婴儿了。

737
00:35:26.810 --> 00:35:28.530
The joke is you can't do it.
笑点是你们做不到。

738
00:35:28.650 --> 00:35:30.150
But we just, I don't know.
但我们就是，我不知道。

739
00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:32.070
We were really, really good at swaddling.
我们真的很擅长包裹婴儿。

740
00:35:32.790 --> 00:35:34.630
They were like, you have to stop.
他们说，你们必须停下来。

741
00:35:34.790 --> 00:35:36.570
You have to stop swaddling that baby.
你们必须停止包裹那个婴儿。

742
00:35:37.010 --> 00:35:39.530
Well, there was a deleted scene after this.
嗯，这之后有个被删减的片段。

743
00:35:39.630 --> 00:35:43.890
I think they were trying to build out the story that the two of you were getting really frustrated
我想他们是想铺垫一个故事，说你们俩变得非常沮丧，

744
00:35:43.890 --> 00:35:45.970
and started to get a little short with one another.
开始对彼此有点不耐烦了。

745
00:35:46.110 --> 00:35:46.790
Oh, I remember.
哦，我记得。

746
00:35:47.130 --> 00:35:49.410
Oh, I felt like we had to hear it.
哦，我觉得我们必须得听听那个。

747
00:35:49.410 --> 00:35:51.570
Pam cusses out Jim.
帕姆咒骂吉姆。

748
00:35:51.990 --> 00:35:54.510
And I think she flips him in the bird at the end.
而且我觉得她在最后还对他竖了中指。

749
00:35:54.590 --> 00:35:55.870
Oh, yeah, she shoots him in the bird.
哦，是的，她对他竖了中指。

750
00:35:56.070 --> 00:35:56.650
I remember.
我记得。

751
00:35:57.450 --> 00:35:59.030
Delivery wasn't so bad, right?
分娩过程没那么糟糕，对吧？

752
00:35:59.610 --> 00:36:00.850
Ah, f*** you.
啊，去你的。

753
00:36:01.710 --> 00:36:02.110
Wow.
哇。

754
00:36:02.430 --> 00:36:03.910
Well, no, I just mean a wonderful ending.
好吧，不，我只是说结局很美好。

755
00:36:04.690 --> 00:36:05.610
Kind of rough getting here.
到这儿的过程有点折腾。

756
00:36:05.770 --> 00:36:06.750
We did not handle that well.
我们当时处理得不太好。

757
00:36:07.130 --> 00:36:09.070
I think you have to admit, you flipped out a little bit.
我觉得你得承认，你当时有点失控了。

758
00:36:10.090 --> 00:36:11.810
I think you should stop talking now.
我觉得你现在最好闭嘴。

759
00:36:12.370 --> 00:36:12.770
Okay.
好吧。

760
00:36:13.510 --> 00:36:14.050
Uh-oh.
噢噢。

761
00:36:14.310 --> 00:36:16.230
Someone's still a little sore.
看来还有人心里不痛快呢。

762
00:36:16.770 --> 00:36:17.850
You sitting on your donut, hon?
亲爱的，你是不是坐在那个甜甜圈坐垫上了？

763
00:36:19.890 --> 00:36:24.650
Okay, so I remember shooting that, and we had a lot of fun with that.
好吧，我记得拍那场戏的时候，我们玩得很开心。

764
00:36:24.790 --> 00:36:25.810
It looks like it.
看起来是这样。

765
00:36:25.870 --> 00:36:34.730
We had a lot of conversations with the people on set who had kids, and they all verified this is a very authentic moment post-birth.
我们和片场那些有孩子的同事聊了很多，他们都证实这确实是产后非常真实的时刻。

766
00:36:36.110 --> 00:36:39.510
It did not end up making it in, but it was pretty fun.
虽然最后没剪进正片，但拍的时候挺有意思的。

767
00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:40.270
It didn't.
确实没剪进去。

768
00:36:40.370 --> 00:36:43.590
You know, in the show notes, it said that it just made Jim seem too mean.
你知道，剧本笔记里说，那会让吉姆显得太刻薄了。

769
00:36:43.810 --> 00:36:46.530
Yes, even though these moments do happen between couples.
没错，尽管夫妻之间确实会发生这种时刻。

770
00:36:46.530 --> 00:36:53.510
They do, but I feel like they left enough in of them being frustrated about, like, breastfeeding, and I think it works.
确实会，但我觉得他们保留了足够多关于母乳喂养感到沮丧的片段，我觉得这样处理很合适。

771
00:36:53.590 --> 00:36:54.150
It works.
很合适。

772
00:36:54.670 --> 00:36:57.110
We got a fan question from Hilde N.
我们收到了一位粉丝希尔德·N的提问。

773
00:36:57.210 --> 00:37:06.470
in Norway, who was curious about the breastfeeding shawl, or whatever it is you call it, that Pam is using in this scene.
她来自挪威，对帕姆在这一幕中使用的哺乳巾，或者不管叫什么的东西感到好奇。

774
00:37:06.470 --> 00:37:14.190
She says, is that to avoid displays of nudity on the show, or is this normal in a U.S.
她问，这是为了避免在剧中出现裸露镜头，还是说这在美国的医院里很常见？

775
00:37:14.330 --> 00:37:14.790
hospital?
医院？

776
00:37:15.390 --> 00:37:16.890
Do women in U.S.
在美国的医院里，

777
00:37:17.010 --> 00:37:20.550
hospitals use these shawls when they are breastfeeding?
女性哺乳时会用这种哺乳巾吗？

778
00:37:21.410 --> 00:37:22.850
I would say no.
我会说不会。

779
00:37:23.070 --> 00:37:24.290
Not in their room.
在病房里不会。

780
00:37:24.510 --> 00:37:25.830
Not in the privacy of their room.
在私密的病房里不会。

781
00:37:25.910 --> 00:37:31.910
But maybe if you were out in a hallway or something, you might have a little blanket or something.
但如果你是在走廊之类的地方，可能会盖个小毯子什么的。

782
00:37:32.210 --> 00:37:33.850
I had one of these shawls.
我当时也有一条这样的哺乳巾。

783
00:37:33.930 --> 00:37:35.490
They're actually really great.
它们其实真的很好用。

784
00:37:35.490 --> 00:37:38.730
I made note of it when I got to use it on the show.
我在剧里用过之后就记住了它。

785
00:37:38.730 --> 00:37:43.050
And when I had my kids in real life, I was like, I want that one that Pam used.
后来我在现实生活中生孩子时，我就想，我想要帕姆用的那种。

786
00:37:43.050 --> 00:37:47.470
because it has this like wire that holds it open
因为它有个钢圈能把它撑开，

787
00:37:47.470 --> 00:37:48.970
so the mom can peek in.
这样妈妈就能往里看。

788
00:37:49.110 --> 00:37:50.210
It was actually really helpful.
它真的非常有帮助。

789
00:37:50.470 --> 00:37:53.790
And I would use one of those for the times
我会在某些时候用它，

790
00:37:53.790 --> 00:37:56.590
that if I had to breastfeed at a restaurant
比如如果我不得不在餐厅哺乳，

791
00:37:56.590 --> 00:37:59.270
or at the airport or wherever,
或者在机场，或者其他什么地方，

792
00:37:59.750 --> 00:38:01.410
maybe if I was in a very public place.
可能是在非常公共的场合。

793
00:38:01.810 --> 00:38:04.070
Although I would like to say there's nothing wrong
虽然我想说，直接拿出来喂也没什么不对，

794
00:38:04.070 --> 00:38:05.410
with just whipping it out, ladies.
女士们。

795
00:38:05.690 --> 00:38:06.670
Your baby's got to eat.
宝宝得吃饭。

796
00:38:06.810 --> 00:38:07.630
Your baby's got to eat.
宝宝得吃饭。

797
00:38:08.170 --> 00:38:11.070
I was such a fan of this one shopping mall
我以前特别喜欢逛一家购物中心，

798
00:38:11.070 --> 00:38:12.930
after Isabel was little that I would go.
伊莎贝尔小时候我常去。

799
00:38:12.930 --> 00:38:17.730
It was like an outdoor mall, and I would have her in her stroller, and we could walk around.
那是个露天商场，我会推着婴儿车带她到处走走。

800
00:38:18.050 --> 00:38:22.690
And for me, it was just being able to get out of the house and get outside a little bit.
对我来说，能走出家门到外面透透气真的很重要。

801
00:38:23.130 --> 00:38:26.650
But I loved it because they had nursing stations.
但我很喜欢，因为他们有哺乳室。

802
00:38:27.110 --> 00:38:28.310
I know what you're talking about.
我知道你在说什么。

803
00:38:28.430 --> 00:38:31.770
They had a little room with a rocking chair in it.
他们有一个带摇椅的小房间。

804
00:38:31.930 --> 00:38:33.690
Yes, and you could go in.
是的，你可以进去。

805
00:38:33.810 --> 00:38:38.990
And so whenever I see a nursing station anywhere, I always smile because I'm like, that is so thoughtful.
所以每当我看到哺乳室，我总是会微笑，因为我觉得这太贴心了。

806
00:38:39.210 --> 00:38:40.570
Now they have them in airports.
现在机场里也有了。

807
00:38:40.570 --> 00:38:43.350
They did not have them in airports when I had my kids.
我生孩子的时候机场可没有。

808
00:38:43.450 --> 00:38:44.510
Yeah, not when we had kids.
是啊，我们生孩子那会儿没有。

809
00:38:44.650 --> 00:38:54.410
But I guess in answer to Hildy's question, we were using that on the show just for the purposes of we couldn't have nudity on television.
不过回答希尔迪的问题，我们在节目里用那个只是因为电视上不能出现裸露镜头。

810
00:38:54.410 --> 00:38:57.990
And also, that was a fakie baby under there.
而且，那下面是个假婴儿。

811
00:38:58.110 --> 00:39:02.750
We needed to limit what you saw of the babies in addition to the boobies.
除了不能露胸部，我们还得限制你看到的婴儿画面。

812
00:39:02.870 --> 00:39:04.210
Also, it was fakie nipple.
而且，那也是个假乳头。

813
00:39:04.390 --> 00:39:08.150
You were wearing that rigged bra with the special pacifier thingy.
你当时穿着那个带有特殊安抚奶嘴装置的特制胸罩。

814
00:39:08.150 --> 00:39:09.150
Oh, my God.
天哪。

815
00:39:09.150 --> 00:39:11.270
I forgot about that, Angela.
我都忘了这事了，安吉拉。

816
00:39:11.610 --> 00:39:12.210
Yes.
是的。

817
00:39:12.590 --> 00:39:15.250
Jenna, on the DVD commentary, you talked about
珍娜，在DVD评论音轨里，你提到过

818
00:39:15.250 --> 00:39:21.690
this elaborate breastfeeding bra rig that they had to build and you wore so it would look like
他们必须制作一套复杂的哺乳胸罩装置，你穿上它，这样看起来

819
00:39:21.690 --> 00:39:22.890
Pam was actually breastfeeding.
帕姆真的在哺乳一样。

820
00:39:23.270 --> 00:39:24.510
I remember that now.
我现在想起来了。

821
00:39:24.710 --> 00:39:27.830
The baby had to want to have their face
婴儿必须要把脸

822
00:39:27.830 --> 00:39:31.990
by my boob, but obviously not near your boob.
贴在我的胸部附近，但显然不能真的靠近你的胸部。

823
00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:33.010
So what do you do?
那你们是怎么做的？

824
00:39:33.190 --> 00:39:34.750
You describe it in the commentary.
你在评论里描述过。

825
00:39:34.750 --> 00:39:35.830
I thought we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

826
00:39:36.350 --> 00:39:38.890
Now, there was like a rig, right, with a pacifier?
当时有个装置，对吧，带个安抚奶嘴？

827
00:39:39.290 --> 00:39:42.910
Oh, it was so complicated, yes, because you wanted the baby to cry,
噢，那太复杂了，是的，因为你既想让婴儿哭，

828
00:39:42.910 --> 00:39:45.710
but then it had to stop crying so you could record our dialogue.
但它又得停止哭泣，这样我们才能录对白。

829
00:39:45.930 --> 00:39:52.050
So they built me a bra that had extra padding so it looked like I was breastfeeding
所以他们给我做了一个胸罩，里面加了衬垫，看起来就像我在哺乳

830
00:39:52.050 --> 00:39:53.930
or my breasts were full of milk.
或者我的乳房涨奶了一样。

831
00:39:54.050 --> 00:40:01.930
But then it also had like a breakaway shield that revealed a sterile nipple pacifier thing.
但它还有一个可拆卸的挡板，露出一个无菌的安抚奶嘴装置。

832
00:40:02.310 --> 00:40:05.790
And then the baby would actually suck on this pacifier and stop crying.
然后婴儿就会真的吸那个奶嘴，停止哭泣。

833
00:40:06.550 --> 00:40:07.570
How about that?
怎么样？

834
00:40:07.790 --> 00:40:16.970
You go to work one day, you get an email, can you build a bra with a pacifier in it that you wore over your clothes?
你某天去上班，收到一封邮件，问能不能做一个带安抚奶嘴的胸罩，还要穿在衣服外面？

835
00:40:17.190 --> 00:40:18.070
Here's the thing.
关键是。

836
00:40:18.310 --> 00:40:20.110
They could change out the pacifier.
他们可以更换那个安抚奶嘴。

837
00:40:20.310 --> 00:40:27.170
They were constantly changing it out with a new sterile pacifier as well so that we'd get nipple change.
他们一直在换新的无菌奶嘴，这样我们就能实现“乳头更换”。

838
00:40:27.350 --> 00:40:28.310
Nipple change.
乳头更换。

839
00:40:28.470 --> 00:40:28.970
Who knew?
谁能想到呢？

840
00:40:29.730 --> 00:40:34.110
Well, in all of this struggle, Jim is going to buzz the nurse.
好吧，在这一团乱中，吉姆要去按护士铃了。

841
00:40:34.910 --> 00:40:37.370
Oh, but I mean, because maybe, did he buzz the nurse?
噢，我是说，因为也许，他是按了护士铃吗？

842
00:40:37.530 --> 00:40:38.690
Maybe Pam sat on it.
也许是帕姆不小心坐到了。

843
00:40:38.910 --> 00:40:40.950
But here she is to help us.
但她现在来帮我们了。

844
00:40:41.790 --> 00:40:46.790
Well, the nurse is going to offer to take baby Cece to the nursery, and they can try again later.
护士提议把小西西带到育婴室，他们稍后再试。

845
00:40:47.010 --> 00:40:47.230
Yeah.
是啊。

846
00:40:47.630 --> 00:40:48.850
And she said, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

847
00:40:48.850 --> 00:40:50.350
If she gets hungry, we'll give her a bottle.
如果她饿了，我们会给她喂奶瓶。

848
00:40:50.490 --> 00:40:51.350
And Pam's like, no, no, no.
帕姆说，不，不，不。

849
00:40:51.630 --> 00:40:52.550
I've heard about this.
我听说过这个。

850
00:40:52.690 --> 00:40:53.970
This is like nipple confusion.
这叫乳头混淆。

851
00:40:54.270 --> 00:40:57.070
Then she'll just want the bottle, and then she won't want to breastfeed.
那她之后就只会想要奶瓶，然后就不愿意母乳喂养了。

852
00:40:57.070 --> 00:41:01.770
And when Pam says this to the nurse, she gets some real nurse sass.
当帕姆对护士说这话时，她遭到了护士的一顿冷嘲热讽。

853
00:41:02.030 --> 00:41:03.690
The nurse is like, oh, good.
护士当时说，哦，真棒。

854
00:41:03.890 --> 00:41:05.010
You know everything.
你什么都懂。

855
00:41:06.550 --> 00:41:12.550
Lady, the line, oh, good, you know everything, is our fan mail flurry.
各位，那句“哦，真棒，你什么都懂”，引发了我们的粉丝来信狂潮。

856
00:41:12.810 --> 00:41:13.230
Really?
真的吗？

857
00:41:13.570 --> 00:41:13.950
Yes.
是的。

858
00:41:14.030 --> 00:41:15.270
That's what set everyone off?
就是那句话让大家都炸锅了？

859
00:41:15.610 --> 00:41:19.410
This phrase really, really bumped people.
这句话真的让很多人感到非常不适。

860
00:41:20.370 --> 00:41:23.030
For example, Alyssa M.
比如，来自犹他州的艾丽莎·M.

861
00:41:23.290 --> 00:41:24.170
from Utah said,
说道，

862
00:41:24.450 --> 00:41:27.270
I'm a postpartum nurse and I love this episode,
我是一名产后护理护士，我很喜欢这一集，

863
00:41:27.470 --> 00:41:30.470
but I always cringe at how the nurse treats Jim and Pam.
但我每次看到护士对待吉姆和帕姆的方式，都感到非常尴尬。

864
00:41:31.050 --> 00:41:33.270
Corey from Rochester, New York said,
来自纽约州罗切斯特的科里说，

865
00:41:34.010 --> 00:41:35.990
Nipple confusion is real.
乳头混淆是真实存在的。

866
00:41:36.230 --> 00:41:38.670
You are the expert because you're the mother.
你是母亲，你才是专家。

867
00:41:39.150 --> 00:41:40.270
Intuition is real.
直觉是真实存在的。

868
00:41:40.490 --> 00:41:42.490
And finally, from Katie G.
最后，来自南卡罗来纳州格林维尔的凯蒂·G.

869
00:41:42.730 --> 00:41:44.270
in Greenville, South Carolina,
说道，

870
00:41:44.770 --> 00:41:47.850
All right, ladies, I have a small soapbox to get on here.
好了，女士们，我要在这里发表一点个人感慨了。

871
00:41:47.850 --> 00:41:50.930
First, I want to really applaud everyone on the show
首先，我要真心称赞剧组的所有人，

872
00:41:50.930 --> 00:41:53.130
for depicting some much more realistic
因为你们展现了更加真实的

873
00:41:53.130 --> 00:41:55.270
pregnancy birth breastfeeding scenes.
怀孕、分娩和母乳喂养的场景。

874
00:41:55.490 --> 00:41:57.290
I love that Pam is scared
我很喜欢帕姆表现出的恐惧，

875
00:41:57.290 --> 00:41:59.550
and showing how long labor can be
也展示了分娩过程可能有多漫长，

876
00:41:59.550 --> 00:42:01.410
and especially how difficult it can be
尤其是展示了掌握母乳喂养

877
00:42:01.410 --> 00:42:02.810
to get the hang of breastfeeding.
有多么困难。

878
00:42:03.130 --> 00:42:06.850
But as for the soapbox, that nurse.
但说到感慨，就是那个护士。

879
00:42:07.010 --> 00:42:07.510
Uh-oh.
噢，不。

880
00:42:07.950 --> 00:42:09.990
Every time I watch this episode,
每次我看这一集时，

881
00:42:10.170 --> 00:42:11.870
I end up fuming at that nurse
我都会对那个护士感到火冒三丈，

882
00:42:11.870 --> 00:42:13.650
for giving Pam sass about,
因为她对帕姆冷嘲热讽，说那句

883
00:42:13.910 --> 00:42:15.190
oh good, you know everything.
“哦，真棒，你什么都懂”。

884
00:42:16.150 --> 00:42:22.610
news alert nipple confusion is real and the mother gets to make the choice as to whether she wants
新闻快讯：乳头混淆是真实存在的，母亲有权选择是否要

885
00:42:22.610 --> 00:42:29.090
her child to have a bottle pacifier anything and that nurse whom in a deleted scene we learn has
让孩子使用奶瓶、安抚奶嘴或任何东西。而那个护士——我们在删减片段中得知她

886
00:42:29.090 --> 00:42:35.330
never had children herself has no right to give pam attitude about her decision katie go off
自己从未生过孩子——根本没权利因为帕姆的决定而对她摆脸色。凯蒂，说得好！

887
00:42:35.330 --> 00:42:40.870
the mama bear in me really wants to storm into that room push that nurse out and assure pam that
我体内的“护犊子”本能真想冲进那个房间，把护士推开，并告诉帕姆

888
00:42:40.870 --> 00:42:42.430
she's doing a wonderful job.
她做得非常棒。

889
00:42:42.770 --> 00:42:44.110
Gah, that nurse.
天哪，那个护士。

890
00:42:45.150 --> 00:42:49.350
She goes on to say, ladies, stand up for yourselves.
她接着说，女士们，要为自己挺身而出。

891
00:42:49.590 --> 00:42:52.850
Don't be bullied and know that you're doing an amazing job regardless.
不要被欺负，要知道无论如何你们都做得非常出色。

892
00:42:53.270 --> 00:42:54.950
Hang in there, mamas.
坚持住，妈妈们。

893
00:42:55.510 --> 00:43:00.570
Thank you for letting me get that off my cheSt. Since my second child is due in mid-October,
谢谢你们让我把心里话说了出来。因为我的第二个孩子预产期在十月中旬，

894
00:43:00.750 --> 00:43:03.810
I'm absolutely keyed up about this issue right now.
我现在对这个问题非常敏感。

895
00:43:04.730 --> 00:43:06.390
Katie, we hear you.
凯蒂，我们听到了你的心声。

896
00:43:06.650 --> 00:43:08.290
Katie, I love you.
凯蒂，我爱你。

897
00:43:08.430 --> 00:43:08.750
Yeah.
没错。

898
00:43:08.750 --> 00:43:12.270
Oh, there is actually one more from Kim E.
哦，其实还有一条来自俄亥俄州的金·E.

899
00:43:12.490 --> 00:43:13.010
in Ohio.
的来信。

900
00:43:13.670 --> 00:43:16.450
Not so much a question as a thank you.
与其说是问题，不如说是一封感谢信。

